{"id":"mahabharata-6-012","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":12,"title":"द्वादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 12 · The island of Shaka and the other dvipas","summary":{"en":"At the king's request Sanjaya gives the size of Jambudvipa and the ocean and describes the Shaka and Kusha islands. He tells of their peoples, seas and sacred mountains.","kn":"ರಾಜನ ಕೋರಿಕೆಯಂತೆ ಸಂಜಯನು ಜಂಬೂದ್ವೀಪ ಮತ್ತು ಸಮುದ್ರದ ವಿಸ್ತಾರವನ್ನು ಹೇಳಿ ಶಾಕದ್ವೀಪ, ಕುಶದ್ವೀಪಗಳನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅಲ್ಲಿಯ ಜನರು, ಸಮುದ್ರಗಳು, ಪವಿತ್ರ ಪರ್ವತಗಳ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"राजा के कहने पर संजय जम्बूद्वीप और समुद्र का विस्तार बताते हैं और शाकद्वीप तथा कुशद्वीप का वर्णन करते हैं। वे वहाँ के लोगों, समुद्रों और पवित्र पर्वतों की चर्चा करते हैं।","te":"రాజు కోరగా సంజయుడు జంబూద్వీపం, సముద్రాల విస్తీర్ణం చెప్పి శాకద్వీపం, కుశద్వీపాలను వర్ణిస్తాడు. అక్కడి ప్రజలు, సముద్రాలు, పవిత్ర పర్వతాల గురించి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"மன்னன் கேட்டபடி சஞ்சயன் ஜம்புத்வீபம், கடல் ஆகியவற்றின் அளவைக் கூறி சாகத்வீபம், குசத்வீபங்களை விவரிக்கிறான். அங்குள்ள மக்கள், கடல்கள், புனித மலைகளைப் பற்றிக் கூறுகிறான்.","ml":"രാജാവിന്റെ ആവശ്യപ്രകാരം ജംബുദ്വീപിന്റെയും സമുദ്രത്തിന്റെയും വലുപ്പം സഞ്ജയൻ പറയുന്നു; ശാകദ്വീപിനെയും കുശദ്വീപിനെയും കുറിച്ചും വിവരിക്കുന്നു. അവിടത്തെ ജനങ്ങളെയും സമുദ്രങ്ങളെയും പുണ്യപർവതങ്ങളെയും കുറിച്ച് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.12; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भूमिपर्व","titleEn":"Bhumi Parva (The earth)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"जम्बूखण्डस्त्वया प्रोक्तो यथावदिह संजय ।\nविष्कम्भमस्य प्रब्रूहि परिमाणं च तत्त्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, you have described the Jambu division properly; now tell me its width and its true measure."}},{"n":2,"text":"समुद्रस्य प्रमाणं च सम्यगच्छिद्रदर्शन ।\nशाकद्वीपं च मे ब्रूहि कुशद्वीपं च संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"You who see without gaps, tell me also the measure of the ocean, and tell me of Shakadvipa and Kushadvipa, Sanjaya."}},{"n":3,"text":"शाल्मलं चैव तत्त्वेन क्रौञ्चद्वीपं तथैव च ।\nब्रूहि गावल्गणे सर्वं राहोः सोमार्कयोस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me truly also of Shalmala and Krauncha island, son of Gavalgana, and of everything concerning Rahu, the moon and the sun."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"राजन्सुबहवो द्वीपा यैरिदं संततं जगत् ।\nसप्त त्वहं प्रवक्ष्यामि चन्द्रादित्यौ ग्रहांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, there are very many islands, by which this world is continuous; I will describe seven of them, and the moon, sun and planets."}},{"n":5,"text":"अष्टादश सहस्राणि योजनानां विशां पते ।\nषट्शतानि च पूर्णानि विष्कम्भो जम्बुपर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the people, the width of Jambu is a full eighteen thousand six hundred yojanas."}},{"n":6,"text":"लावणस्य समुद्रस्य विष्कम्भो द्विगुणः स्मृतः ।\nनानाजनपदाकीर्णो मणिविद्रुमचित्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The width of the salt sea is said to be double, strewn with many countries and pictured with gems and coral."}},{"n":7,"text":"नैकधातुविचित्रैश्च पर्वतैरुपशोभितः ।\nसिद्धचारणसंकीर्णः सागरः परिमण्डलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is adorned with mountains varied with many minerals, and the circular sea is crowded with Siddhas and Charanas."}},{"n":8,"text":"शाकद्वीपं च वक्ष्यामि यथावदिह पार्थिव ।\nशृणु मे त्वं यथान्यायं ब्रुवतः कुरुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now, King, I will describe Shakadvipa as it truly is; listen to me, descendant of Kuru, as I tell it in due order."}},{"n":9,"text":"जम्बूद्वीपप्रमाणेन द्विगुणः स नराधिप ।\nविष्कम्भेण महाराज सागरोऽपि विभागशः ।\nक्षीरोदो भरतश्रेष्ठ येन संपरिवारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, that island is twice Jambudvipa in width, and so is its sea, section by section, the Ocean of Milk, by which it is surrounded, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":10,"text":"तत्र पुण्या जनपदा न तत्र म्रियते जनः ।\nकुत एव हि दुर्भिक्षं क्षमातेजोयुता हि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its countries are holy and no people die there; how could there be famine, when they are full of patience and vigour?"}},{"n":11,"text":"शाकद्वीपस्य संक्षेपो यथावद्भरतर्षभ ।\nउक्त एष महाराज किमन्यच्छ्रोतुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Bharatas, I have told you the summary of Shakadvipa as it is; what else do you wish to hear?"}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"शाकद्वीपस्य संक्षेपो यथावदिह संजय ।\nउक्तस्त्वया महाभाग विस्तरं ब्रूहि तत्त्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, you have given the summary of Shakadvipa truly; now, blessed one, tell me in detail and truly."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"तथैव पर्वता राजन्सप्तात्र मणिभूषिताः ।\nरत्नाकरास्तथा नद्यस्तेषां नामानि मे शृणु ।\nअतीवगुणवत्सर्वं तत्र पुण्यं जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, in the same way there are here seven mountains adorned with gems, and rivers that are mines of jewels; hear their names from me. Everything there is exceedingly excellent and holy, lord of the people."}},{"n":14,"text":"देवर्षिगन्धर्वयुतः परमो मेरुरुच्यते ।\nप्रागायतो महाराज मलयो नाम पर्वतः ।\nयतो मेघाः प्रवर्तन्ते प्रभवन्ति च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The supreme Meru, frequented by divine sages and Gandharvas, is spoken of; stretching east to west is the mountain called Malaya, from which clouds arise and spread everywhere."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततः परेण कौरव्य जलधारो महागिरिः ।\nयत्र नित्यमुपादत्ते वासवः परमं जलम् ।\nयतो वर्षं प्रभवति वर्षाकाले जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beyond it, descendant of Kuru, is the great mountain Jaladhara, where Indra always draws the best water, from which rain comes in the rainy season, lord of men."}},{"n":16,"text":"उच्चैर्गिरी रैवतको यत्र नित्यं प्रतिष्ठितः ।\nरेवती दिवि नक्षत्रं पितामहकृतो विधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There stands the high mountain Raivataka, where the star Revati is fixed in the sky, an arrangement made by the Grandsire."}},{"n":17,"text":"उत्तरेण तु राजेन्द्र श्यामो नाम महागिरिः ।\nयतः श्यामत्वमापन्नाः प्रजा जनपदेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"To the north, king of kings, is the great mountain called Shyama, from which the people of the land became dark, lord of the country."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"सुमहान्संशयो मेऽद्य प्रोक्तं संजय यत्त्वया ।\nप्रजाः कथं सूतपुत्र संप्राप्ताः श्यामतामिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, I have a very great doubt about what you said; how, son of the charioteer, did the people come to be dark?"}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"सर्वेष्वेव महाप्राज्ञ द्वीपेषु कुरुनन्दन ।\nगौरः कृष्णश्च वर्णौ द्वौ तयोर्वर्णान्तरं नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great sage, descendant of Kuru, in all the islands there are two colours, fair and dark, and between them there is a difference of hue."}},{"n":20,"text":"श्यामो यस्मात्प्रवृत्तो वै तत्ते वक्ष्यामि भारत ।\nआस्तेऽत्र भगवान्कृष्णस्तत्कान्त्या श्यामतां गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will tell you, Bharata, how the darkness arose. The blessed Krishna dwells here, and by his lustre it became dark."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः परं कौरवेन्द्र दुर्गशैलो महोदयः ।\nकेसरी केसरयुतो यतो वातः प्रवायति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beyond it, best of the Kauravas, is the high and prosperous mountain Durga, and Kesari, rich in kesara flowers, from where the wind blows."}},{"n":22,"text":"तेषां योजनविष्कम्भो द्विगुणः प्रविभागशः ।\nवर्षाणि तेषु कौरव्य संप्रोक्तानि मनीषिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For these mountains the width in yojanas doubles in each division, and the wise have declared the regions in them, descendant of Kuru."}},{"n":23,"text":"महामेरुर्महाकाशो जलदः कुमुदोत्तरः ।\nजलधारात्परो राजन्सुकुमार इति स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are Mahameru, Mahakasha, Jalada and Kumudottara; beyond Jaladhara, King, the region is called Sukumara."}},{"n":24,"text":"रैवतस्य तु कौमारः श्यामस्य तु मणीचकः ।\nकेसरस्याथ मोदाकी परेण तु महापुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kaumara belongs to Raivata, Manichaka to Shyama, Modaki to Kesari, and beyond that is Mahapuman."}},{"n":25,"text":"परिवार्य तु कौरव्य दैर्घ्यं ह्रस्वत्वमेव च ।\nजम्बूद्वीपेन विख्यातस्तस्य मध्ये महाद्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Encircling them, descendant of Kuru, are length and shortness; as with Jambudvipa, in its middle stands a great tree."}},{"n":26,"text":"शाको नाम महाराज तस्य द्वीपस्य मध्यगः ।\nतत्र पुण्या जनपदाः पूज्यते तत्र शंकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, the tree called Shaka stands in the middle of that island, and there are holy countries, where Shankara is worshipped."}},{"n":27,"text":"तत्र गच्छन्ति सिद्धाश्च चारणा दैवतानि च ।\nधार्मिकाश्च प्रजा राजंश्चत्वारोऽतीव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Siddhas, Charanas and divine beings go there, King, and the people are exceedingly righteous in all four classes, Bharata."}},{"n":28,"text":"वर्णाः स्वकर्मनिरता न च स्तेनोऽत्र दृश्यते ।\nदीर्घायुषो महाराज जरामृत्युविवर्जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The classes are devoted to their own duties and no thief is seen there; the people are long-lived, great king, free from old age and death."}},{"n":29,"text":"प्रजास्तत्र विवर्धन्ते वर्षास्विव समुद्रगाः ।\nनद्यः पुण्यजलास्तत्र गङ्गा च बहुधागतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The people there flourish like rivers running to the sea in the rains; holy-watered rivers are there, and the Ganga with many courses."}},{"n":30,"text":"सुकुमारी कुमारी च सीता कावेरका तथा ।\nमहानदी च कौरव्य तथा मणिजला नदी ।\nइक्षुवर्धनिका चैव तथा भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sukumari, Kumari, Sita, Kaveraka, and the great river, descendant of Kuru, the river Manijala and Ikshuvardhanika, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततः प्रवृत्ताः पुण्योदा नद्यः कुरुकुलोद्वह ।\nसहस्राणां शतान्येव यतो वर्षति वासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From them, bearer of the Kuru line, flow rivers with holy water, hundreds of thousands, wherever Indra sends rain."}},{"n":32,"text":"न तासां नामधेयानि परिमाणं तथैव च ।\nशक्यते परिसंख्यातुं पुण्यास्ता हि सरिद्वराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their names and their number cannot be counted, for those great rivers are holy."}},{"n":33,"text":"तत्र पुण्या जनपदाश्चत्वारो लोकसंमताः ।\nमगाश्च मशकाश्चैव मानसा मन्दगास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are four holy countries there, honoured by the world: the Magas, Mashakas, Manasas and Mandagas."}},{"n":34,"text":"मगा ब्राह्मणभूयिष्ठाः स्वकर्मनिरता नृप ।\nमशकेषु तु राजन्या धार्मिकाः सर्वकामदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Magas are mostly Brahmins devoted to their own duties, King; among the Mashakas are kings, righteous and granting all wishes."}},{"n":35,"text":"मानसेषु महाराज वैश्याः कर्मोपजीविनः ।\nसर्वकामसमायुक्ताः शूरा धर्मार्थनिश्चिताः ।\nशूद्रास्तु मन्दगे नित्यं पुरुषा धर्मशीलिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, in the Manasas are Vaishyas who live by their work, endowed with all desires, brave and firm in dharma and wealth; and in Mandaga are Shudras, always men of virtuous conduct."}},{"n":36,"text":"न तत्र राजा राजेन्द्र न दण्डो न च दण्डिकाः ।\nस्वधर्मेणैव धर्मं च ते रक्षन्ति परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, king of kings, there is no king, no punishment and no punishers; by their own dharma alone they guard dharma among themselves."}},{"n":37,"text":"एतावदेव शक्यं तु तस्मिन्द्वीपे प्रभाषितुम् ।\nएतावदेव श्रोतव्यं शाकद्वीपे महौजसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is all that can be said of that island; this much is to be heard of the mighty Shakadvipa."}}]}]}